main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ begin/end layout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ argument: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
Invariant check failed
--
The MSVC STL's std::initializer_list holds a begin and an end pointer;
building one from a braced list stored the size into the end pointer
(from_integer precondition), 26 failures on VS 2022.  clang++ accepts this
program; g++ insists on its own layout.
